      },
      "cr": 2,
      "biography": {
        "value": "<p><em>Waluipedia cast sheet — The Plant of the Manor.</em> Built by <code>tools/build-character-sheets.py</code>, generated from the article's own words. no XP ledger entry; archetype default → CR 2 as a monster. Numbers are a GM-ready reading of the record, not a filed stat line; the article stays the authority. Archive date 1040 BF.</p><p><strong>The Thing Wearing Lady Aurelian, and What Was Under the Face</strong> — The overgrowth of the Overgrown Manor / claimant to the manor by right of growth</p><p>Status: Destroyed as a face, ascendant as a thing - the glamour broke in the sanctuary room; the floor opened under it</p><p>The overgrowth's masterpiece: a plant that wore Lady Aurelian Corvinarus well enough to hold a conversation over cold tea, run a household, and issue standing orders to guards who never questioned them. Confronted in its own sanctuary, it explained its plan - collapse the manor, let trees grow in the ruins - took a bowl of Red's poisoned kitchen slop to the chest, and came apart into something with roots in its eye sockets.</p><h3>Evidence</h3><ul><li><strong>Claws</strong> — “The Thing Wearing Lady Aurelian, and What Was Under the Face”</li><li><strong>Grasping Growth</strong> — “Confronted in its own sanctuary, it explained its plan - collapse the manor, let trees grow in the ruins - took a bowl of Red's poisoned kitchen slop to the chest, and came apart into something with roots in its eye”</li><li><strong>Puzzle Discipline</strong> — “Asked why it bothered impersonating the lady rather than simply killing everyone, it said it needed to move some puzzle pieces into place, and then it said the line this archive will be quoting for a year - the beauty”</li></ul><p>Article: <code>#/article/the_plant_lady</code> (characters). Site sheet: <code>#/sheets/the_plant_lady</code>.</p>",
        "public": ""
      }
    },
